WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:04.810
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

00:04.810 --> 00:12.530
Asano hitogomi o nagamete coffee nondeiru
Watching a crowd in the morning, and drinking coffee

00:13.450 --> 00:21.450
Aseri nado naikano youni hitoni wa mieru daro
People must see me as if I don't have any worries

00:22.080 --> 00:29.920
lma menomae ni atomodori dekinai jikan ga
I know that the time I will never be able to get back

00:30.710 --> 00:38.220
Tashika ni nagareteru koto o watashi wa shitteru
Is moving in front of me

00:38.430 --> 00:47.440
Marude kyou shika nai toiu ikikata o shitemita toki
If I live like today is the last day of my life

00:47.730 --> 00:55.490
Saisho ni nani ga mieru darou
I wonder what I can see first

00:56.570 --> 01:00.830
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

01:01.240 --> 01:09.250
Sore ga donnani chiisana hikari demo ii
I don't care no matter how small the light is

01:09.750 --> 01:11.750
Sugata o misete hoshii
I just wish to see its shape

01:11.750 --> 01:16.010
Oh please come down like an angel
Oh please come down like an angel

01:16.680 --> 01:22.390
lma no kimochi sonomama hanaseru
I want to meet someone

01:22.390 --> 01:22.680
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Mermaid Forest
lma no kimochi sonomama hanaseru
I want to meet someone

01:22.680 --> 01:29.190
Mermaid Forest
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Sonna hito ni deaitai
Who I can tell my honest feelings to

01:29.190 --> 01:30.980
Mermaid Forest
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology

01:37.400 --> 01:39.430
Yuta, what's that?

01:39.870 --> 01:41.030
A yacht.

01:50.820 --> 01:51.980
It feels nice.

02:02.560 --> 02:04.090
Yuta, what's the matter?

02:04.200 --> 02:06.630
Oh, it's nothing.

02:07.730 --> 02:08.530
I see.

02:14.570 --> 02:17.130
<i>It was a nice dream, Rin.</i>

02:25.540 --> 02:30.040
Episode 2
Village of the Fighting Fish
(Part I)

02:39.000 --> 02:42.130
Trouble!
Pirates!

02:45.000 --> 02:46.330
Pirates!

02:49.210 --> 02:50.640
You thieves!

02:50.640 --> 02:53.540
You think you can pass
through without paying?

03:10.800 --> 03:12.920
Please spare us.

03:13.170 --> 03:15.360
You can take all the cargo!

03:18.070 --> 03:21.040
You idiots!
You got it all wrong!

03:22.810 --> 03:27.400
We came to talk.
These are our waters around here.

03:27.780 --> 03:31.010
Isn't it only fair that
we ask you to pay a toll?

03:31.820 --> 03:33.790
Give us 10% of your cargo.

03:35.050 --> 03:37.390
Huh? That's it?

03:38.220 --> 03:41.390
Of course!
We're not thieves.

03:44.800 --> 03:49.100
It feels nice to work in moderation.

03:50.440 --> 03:52.840
Being moderate about
everything is the best way.

04:02.580 --> 04:06.020
Hey, there go the people of Toba!

04:06.120 --> 04:09.250
Meager earnings you've
got there, as usual!

04:10.520 --> 04:12.360
The bunch from Sakagami Island.

04:12.360 --> 04:12.960
Damn.

04:12.960 --> 04:14.760
Imagine running into
those bastards here.

04:15.190 --> 04:17.560
Rin!
How's your old man?

04:17.800 --> 04:20.200
Still alive and kicking!

04:20.300 --> 04:21.430
Is he?

04:21.430 --> 04:26.000
I haven't seen him at all these days.
I was sure he had died.

04:28.740 --> 04:32.180
Shut up!
Be gone or we'll kill you!

04:32.340 --> 04:33.970
You'll kill us?

04:34.150 --> 04:37.910
Have you got the guts to kill?

04:38.150 --> 04:40.080
Give it your best shot.

04:40.820 --> 04:42.750
Look at their cargo.

04:43.190 --> 04:43.920
Yeah.

04:44.420 --> 04:45.960
All covered in blood.

04:45.960 --> 04:47.520
That's awful.

04:47.790 --> 04:50.930
They must have wiped out everyone
on board the boat they raided.

04:50.930 --> 04:51.760
Yeah.

04:56.700 --> 04:58.600
Oh, they're back!

04:58.600 --> 04:59.090
Ah, all right!

05:04.340 --> 05:05.210
Pull!

05:05.210 --> 05:05.910
Ho!

05:05.910 --> 05:07.480
Pull harder!

05:07.480 --> 05:08.070
Ho!

05:08.350 --> 05:09.410
Dear.

05:09.410 --> 05:10.120
Hey.

05:10.120 --> 05:11.280
Dad!

05:11.280 --> 05:12.410
Yeah.

05:12.550 --> 05:14.180
Come now.
Help carry the load!

05:15.050 --> 05:16.850
Big sister Rin!

05:17.960 --> 05:19.550
Big sister!

05:20.590 --> 05:21.960
A body?

05:22.130 --> 05:22.790
Yeah.

05:22.930 --> 05:25.160
We just went to check the net.

05:25.530 --> 05:28.190
Again?
What the hell.

05:35.440 --> 05:37.930
Oh, he's completely gone.

05:38.040 --> 05:39.980
He's not from around here.

05:40.150 --> 05:41.870
Dying at such a young age.

05:42.050 --> 05:45.570
But look at how peaceful he looks.

05:46.020 --> 05:47.710
He looks like he's sleeping.

05:48.020 --> 05:48.880
No.

05:49.320 --> 05:52.050
He's not breathing.
His body's completely cold.

05:52.760 --> 05:53.690
Let's bury him in the ground.

05:54.030 --> 05:54.680
Yes, ma'am.

05:59.430 --> 06:00.020
Let's go.

06:17.020 --> 06:18.050
Rin?

06:18.050 --> 06:20.450
Yeah, Dad, I'm home.

06:21.520 --> 06:24.150
I heard commotion on the beach.

06:24.860 --> 06:27.090
Another dead body washed up.

06:28.460 --> 06:31.330
One after another, it's like an
endless stream these days.

06:31.630 --> 06:35.690
And sometimes it's one of the
pirates from the Sakagami Island.

06:37.900 --> 06:38.960
Hey, Dad.

06:41.770 --> 06:44.070
Do you think there
really are mermaids?

06:44.880 --> 06:49.580
I don't know, I only heard stories.

06:52.050 --> 06:55.450
It seems the Sakagami
are looking for mermaids.

06:56.090 --> 06:57.110
Mermaids?

06:58.890 --> 07:01.830
They say you obtain eternal youth and
immortality by eating mermaid flesh.

07:02.090 --> 07:06.220
If that's true, we have to stop them
before they get their hands on it.

07:07.300 --> 07:10.060
What would you do
if you got a hold of some?

07:11.100 --> 07:12.640
I'll have you eat it!

07:12.640 --> 07:15.660
Then your illness will
be instantly cured.

07:19.980 --> 07:22.310
Has it been hard carrying
on in my place?

07:23.380 --> 07:28.010
Everyone seems to acknowledge
you as a competent young Chief.

07:29.550 --> 07:31.680
I'm not as good as you, but...

07:41.930 --> 07:43.760
Sister!

07:46.000 --> 07:47.840
You picked a lot of them, Sayori.

07:47.840 --> 07:50.430
Yeah, I'm going to give
them to the dead people.

07:50.610 --> 07:52.010
Want to come with us?

08:05.820 --> 08:08.490
<i>Do mermaids really exist?</i>

08:09.860 --> 08:13.520
<i>The scales that are washed</i>
<i>ashore along with these people...</i>

08:26.850 --> 08:30.010
<i>Are they mermaid scales?</i>

08:31.280 --> 08:34.910
Oh, the flowers we planted
the other day have taken root!

08:35.450 --> 08:36.580
Over here, too!

08:37.120 --> 08:41.250
Wow, this place will be
covered with flowers soon!

08:41.490 --> 08:42.360
Yeah.

08:43.090 --> 08:45.060
That's not something
to be happy about.

08:46.430 --> 08:49.030
This is the dead man we found today.

08:49.970 --> 08:52.730
Yeah. Give them here.
I'll plant them for you.

08:54.270 --> 08:56.240
They die and become fertilizer.

08:56.640 --> 08:58.840
Human beings are pathetic creatures.

09:16.360 --> 09:18.060
Stay back, you bastard!

09:21.900 --> 09:24.370
Wait!
I'm not going to hurt you!

09:25.540 --> 09:27.600
What?
How dare you!

09:28.070 --> 09:29.670
No, Sister!

09:29.670 --> 09:32.170
If it hits him, he'll die again!
Don't!

09:41.290 --> 09:43.810
I'm Yuta.

09:44.660 --> 09:47.280
The guy we buried yesterday
came back to life!

09:47.430 --> 09:49.830
He's gone to the Chief
to pay his respects!

09:50.100 --> 09:51.560
Wow, let's go see!

09:53.000 --> 09:56.930
I see.
You must have very good luck.

09:57.340 --> 10:01.000
Thank you. It seems your people
even gave me a memorial service.

10:01.640 --> 10:02.870
Are you a fisherman?

10:03.210 --> 10:04.900
Yes, I used to be.

10:05.440 --> 10:09.880
But I'm just a wanderer now, working on
a boat or fighting someone else's war.

10:10.580 --> 10:12.240
I do anything for hire.

10:13.250 --> 10:14.780
On that day, at the port...

10:17.160 --> 10:18.420
<i>You...</i>

10:20.860 --> 10:22.830
<i>Are you interested</i>
<i>in mermaid hunting?</i>

10:26.100 --> 10:28.690
Oh, a woman?

10:30.500 --> 10:34.060
Was it a slimy,
sleazy woman of about 30?

10:34.810 --> 10:35.970
You know her?

10:35.970 --> 10:36.700
Yeah.

10:36.910 --> 10:41.110
It must be Isago, the wife of
the Chief of the Sakagami Pirates.

10:50.160 --> 10:51.460
No good.

10:51.460 --> 10:54.650
I hired about half a dozen young
ones at the port the other day...

10:55.160 --> 10:56.790
but none of them have come back.

10:57.000 --> 10:58.860
Humph, damn them.

10:59.760 --> 11:02.060
They must've died,
getting caught in a whirlpool.

11:02.730 --> 11:06.670
Big sister, are you sure there
really are mermaids in the world?

11:07.410 --> 11:08.510
Sure there are.

11:08.510 --> 11:10.740
There were a lot of them
where I come from.

11:11.410 --> 11:13.970
They say you can get eternal
youth and immortality, but...

11:14.410 --> 11:17.250
What good is it, if you go to catch
mermaids and die in the process?

11:26.390 --> 11:30.790
We haven't caught them
because you're such cowards!

11:31.700 --> 11:33.200
Oh, man...

11:33.200 --> 11:34.390
He's dead.

11:35.500 --> 11:38.440
Human life is fragile indeed.

11:40.070 --> 11:42.270
Aren't you sad?

11:42.710 --> 11:45.840
Don't you want to obtain
eternal youth and immortality?

11:49.930 --> 11:59.940
Rumiko Takahashi Anthology
Mermaid Forest

12:10.340 --> 12:13.000
Miss Rin,
thank you for standing guard.

12:13.270 --> 12:13.790
Yeah.

12:26.720 --> 12:27.810
That bastard.

12:28.420 --> 12:29.350
Stop right there!

12:30.220 --> 12:31.050
You!

12:50.540 --> 12:51.440
You idiot!

12:51.440 --> 12:53.910
What are you doing jumping
into the water while wearing armor?

12:55.680 --> 12:56.350
Ouch!

12:56.350 --> 12:57.640
You boat thief!

13:01.690 --> 13:03.920
I apologize for taking
the boat without asking.

13:04.420 --> 13:07.080
If you want to get back to port,
why didn't you just say so?

13:08.290 --> 13:10.260
I wanted to go back to that place...

13:10.530 --> 13:12.760
the place where they
say mermaids live.

13:15.900 --> 13:18.270
I thought you were just hired muscle...

13:19.000 --> 13:22.010
but I guess you're just like the others,
looking for eternal youth and immortality.

13:22.010 --> 13:22.900
To hell with that.

13:24.480 --> 13:28.100
I don't mean to brag, but this is
the fifth time I've come back to life.

13:28.850 --> 13:30.970
That's something to
brag about all right.

13:31.750 --> 13:33.720
Then you...

13:35.290 --> 13:39.880
Yeah. I ate mermaid flesh
a long time ago.

13:44.600 --> 13:48.560
Then, there's no need for you
to look for mermaids anymore.

13:49.330 --> 13:51.860
I just want to become
a normal human.

13:53.340 --> 13:57.740
I've been killed in war,
and I've drowned to death.

13:58.480 --> 14:00.440
It's so painful and agonizing.

14:01.250 --> 14:03.910
I'd think, oh this is the end of it all,
but then I just come back to life again.

14:05.380 --> 14:07.350
It's pretty tough.

14:07.450 --> 14:10.390
I heard I have to find a
mermaid to return to normal.

14:10.690 --> 14:12.490
Hey, where can you find them?

14:12.620 --> 14:13.780
Why do you want to know?

14:14.460 --> 14:17.090
I don't know how long you've lived...

14:17.600 --> 14:19.650
but you don't know squat
about the waters around here.

14:19.860 --> 14:22.130
I can't stand the thought
of you sailing out alone...

14:22.130 --> 14:23.500
and wrecking the boat.

14:24.200 --> 14:25.900
You're going to let me use it?

14:27.810 --> 14:30.870
Like this. Looking at this
mountain on the right...

14:31.580 --> 14:32.840
go a little way out to sea.

14:33.510 --> 14:34.600
It's around here.

14:37.080 --> 14:40.410
If we tide our way from this island,
we might be able to make it.

14:42.090 --> 14:43.580
But this isn't a good time.

14:43.690 --> 14:45.920
Wait for a while until
the first quarter moon.

14:46.890 --> 14:49.290
I can't let you use
the boat for free. Work!

14:49.790 --> 14:50.850
OK.

14:52.330 --> 14:54.730
I may not look like it, but
I was a pretty good fisherman.

14:56.800 --> 14:58.390
OK, let's go!

15:09.680 --> 15:11.310
You guys always do this?

15:11.520 --> 15:13.210
We fish, too.

15:13.550 --> 15:15.920
Isn't this an act of piracy?

15:16.350 --> 15:17.340
You think?

15:18.020 --> 15:20.150
It's a toll.
A toll!

15:20.560 --> 15:21.990
Yes. Yes. That's right.

15:35.270 --> 15:36.470
You're something.

15:38.780 --> 15:40.740
He seems to be getting
used to life in this village.

15:41.480 --> 15:43.740
Yeah, he's a hard working man.

15:50.920 --> 15:54.150
Yuta, Tohkichi, come with me.
We're going to the market at the port.

15:56.330 --> 15:58.520
You look pretty, sister!

16:04.600 --> 16:05.160
What?

16:05.740 --> 16:08.760
Oh, that outfit is very becoming.

16:09.340 --> 16:11.040
Yeah, you look beautiful.

16:11.940 --> 16:13.570
Don't be stupid.

16:23.860 --> 16:24.750
Hey, Yuta.

16:26.720 --> 16:30.060
Would you stay on our island
if you could return to normal?

16:31.060 --> 16:33.330
Yeah.
If I can return to normal.

16:45.510 --> 16:47.980
Tohkichi, don't go too far.

16:48.380 --> 16:49.740
I know!

16:50.620 --> 16:51.640
There.

16:52.420 --> 16:56.150
Hey, mister, why don't you buy this?
See, it's unusual, isn't it?

16:56.590 --> 16:57.950
No thanks.

16:58.120 --> 17:01.060
It sparkles when you hold it
up to the sun. It's really...

17:02.230 --> 17:03.220
Boy.

17:03.430 --> 17:05.830
Where did you get this?

17:08.100 --> 17:09.960
It's such a pretty scale.

17:10.770 --> 17:11.430
Yeah!

17:12.000 --> 17:14.770
How about this comb?
For 20 sardines.

17:15.210 --> 17:16.040
Fifteen sardines.

17:16.540 --> 17:17.740
Sister!

17:18.740 --> 17:20.640
I sold that scale.

17:21.010 --> 17:22.910
Someone really bought that thing?

17:28.350 --> 17:29.410
Isago!

17:30.220 --> 17:34.520
Oh, what a surprise.
You came back alive.

17:34.990 --> 17:36.760
He came back to life!

17:36.830 --> 17:37.620
Tohkichi!

17:41.300 --> 17:43.630
So, did you find any mermaids?

17:43.940 --> 17:44.770
No.

17:46.200 --> 17:50.800
Then how could you come back alive?

17:58.150 --> 18:00.170
You ate mermaid flesh, didn't you?

18:02.790 --> 18:04.550
You!
Leave him alone!!

18:04.890 --> 18:06.790
If you keep making a
stupid accusation like that!

18:07.290 --> 18:08.620
Sorry.

18:09.730 --> 18:10.790
This hair pin.

18:11.030 --> 18:12.090
I'll take it.

18:12.200 --> 18:12.890
OK.

18:13.970 --> 18:15.090
A token of apology.

18:15.370 --> 18:16.460
You can have it.

18:21.870 --> 18:22.640
Forget it!

18:25.510 --> 18:27.840
Doesn't it hurt?
Doesn't it hurt?

18:28.580 --> 18:29.740
Yes, it does!

18:45.230 --> 18:47.820
Rin told me what happened today.

18:48.970 --> 18:51.160
A terrible thing that
woman did to you.

18:52.670 --> 18:54.270
Those fools.

18:54.270 --> 18:58.230
Why can't they be satisfied
with the lives given to them?

18:58.840 --> 19:03.610
To eat modestly, to work modestly,
and to live modestly.

19:04.920 --> 19:06.880
Well, in our case...

19:07.080 --> 19:10.250
we're compelled to steal
modestly in order to survive.

19:14.190 --> 19:16.060
What do you think of Rin?

19:16.990 --> 19:18.120
What do I think?

19:19.360 --> 19:20.990
I don't have long to live.

19:22.530 --> 19:25.400
What I'm concerned about
is my three children.

19:26.400 --> 19:28.430
Especially Rin.

19:29.910 --> 19:33.040
She's leading this
island courageously...

19:33.040 --> 19:36.140
waiting for the day that her brother,
Tohkichi, becomes a man.

19:36.750 --> 19:38.720
But a woman is still a woman.

19:39.750 --> 19:41.720
I want you to marry her.

19:44.020 --> 19:47.320
Rin's very fond of you.
You can live here.

19:49.290 --> 19:51.260
<i>If I can become a normal human...</i>

19:53.360 --> 19:54.760
Go to bed.

19:54.900 --> 19:56.390
You have to get up early
tomorrow, as usual.

19:56.500 --> 19:58.090
Yes, well then...

20:04.010 --> 20:04.980
Isago.

20:07.310 --> 20:12.310
The wound on your
hand has healed, hasn't it?

20:16.290 --> 20:18.260
So you did eat it.

20:19.160 --> 20:20.450
Mermaid flesh.

20:23.230 --> 20:27.160
Yeah, I did.
But it was long time ago.

20:27.670 --> 20:30.330
Don't lie to me!
You're hiding it somewhere!

20:32.700 --> 20:34.800
What are you trying to do,
swinging that thing around?

20:35.710 --> 20:37.200
I won't die.

20:45.580 --> 20:46.410
Dad!

20:48.250 --> 20:50.380
He still seems to be
holding onto life.

20:51.120 --> 20:54.150
He'll live if you feed
him mermaid flesh.

20:55.660 --> 20:57.090
Dad! Dad!

20:57.400 --> 20:58.730
Don't shake him, Rin!

21:01.630 --> 21:05.260
He's all right. He won't die
from a scratch like this.

21:06.070 --> 21:07.630
I wonder.

21:08.140 --> 21:10.570
He looked pretty weak
from the illness.

21:12.680 --> 21:14.650
Isago!

21:15.850 --> 21:17.400
How dare you hurt my father!

21:28.830 --> 21:30.120
She's gone.

21:33.200 --> 21:34.260
Rin!

21:34.330 --> 21:34.920
Rin!

21:35.470 --> 21:39.400
<i>Don't die, Dad! I'll be right back</i>
<i>with mermaid flesh!</i>

21:41.140 --> 21:42.500
Rin, wait!

21:42.770 --> 21:43.930
What's going on, Yuta?

21:44.180 --> 21:45.280
It's so late!

21:45.280 --> 21:46.680
Take care of the Chief!

21:46.680 --> 21:48.170
-What?
-The Chief!

22:02.360 --> 22:05.560
<i>Mermaid, I'll find you</i>
<i>no matter what!</i>

22:25.030 --> 22:33.540
Mukashi no koto datowa mada katazuke rarenai
It's just something in the past, but I still can't forget it

22:34.910 --> 22:43.420
ltsumade kakaruno to anata wa warau kedo
"How long does it take?" You smiled at me

22:44.880 --> 22:53.760
Dorekurai oboete iru hidoku naki nagara
How much do you remember? I cried hard

22:54.810 --> 23:04.320
Dorekurai oboete iru anokoto to ieba
How much do you remember if I talk about "that thing"?

23:09.450 --> 23:18.460
ltsumademo mada utsumuite
I still look down

23:19.420 --> 23:27.920
Tobikoe rarenai mizutamari
I can't jump over the puddle

23:29.050 --> 23:38.560
Wakaranakunaru moshikasuruto
I'm confused

23:38.890 --> 23:48.400
Kawarenai no wa watashi dake kana
Maybe I'm the only one who still can't change

23:53.320 --> 24:02.880
Mukashi no koto datowa mada katazuke rarenai
It's just something in the past, but I still can't forget it

24:06.150 --> 24:08.550
Rin and I finally catch a mermaid.

24:08.720 --> 24:10.750
But we are attacked
by the pirates of Sakagami...

24:10.750 --> 24:12.490
who were just waiting
for us to catch one.

24:12.490 --> 24:14.490
Stabbed by a few dozen harpoons...

24:14.490 --> 24:16.590
the mermaid and I lose
our strength in the storm.

24:16.590 --> 24:19.260
The Chief of Sakagami eats
mermaid flesh and becomes immortal.

24:19.260 --> 24:21.300
But something starts
happening to his body.

24:21.300 --> 24:24.500
And, the Chief's wife, Isago,
who also eats the mermaid flesh...

24:24.940 --> 24:27.030
What is she up to?

24:27.370 --> 24:29.810
What's the real secret
of the mermaids?

24:30.240 --> 24:30.990
